  "origin": "PROTOTYPE record demonstrating a proposed solution to Gap B (per-document multi-license aggregate). Same source as pleias-common-corpus-github-opensource.jsonld but with `license` as an array of `{ iri, count, proportion }` entries instead of a single IRI. This faithfully represents that the OpenSource collection is NOT uniformly MIT-licensed — it aggregates GitHub repositories carrying different permissive SPDX licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, CC0, and others). NOTE: the `license`-as-array shape is NOT part of the 0.0.1 schema — this record will NOT validate against the current schema as-is; it is intentionally a forward-looking prototype. The `count` and `proportion` values are 0.0 placeholders because exact per-license counts are not published per-collection in the Common Corpus metadata; a real entry would carry the true counts (or be computed from the dataset's per-document `license` field). See notes/stress-test-pleias-common-corpus.md (Gap B proposed direction).",
